.TH SB\-DAEMON 1 "2026-11-07" "sb-daemon" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
sb\-daemon \- SteadyBearing fan control daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sb\-daemon
[\fB\-\-socket\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-db\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sb\-daemon
samples CPU temperature, CPU usage, fan RPM and PWM from
.IR /sys/class/hwmon ,
runs a hysteresis fan curve, and stores tiered telemetry history in SQLite.
It restores automatic fan control on SIGTERM or shutdown.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-socket\-path \fIPATH\fR
Unix socket to listen on. Defaults to
.IR /run/sb/sb.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-db\-path \fIPATH\fR
History database. Defaults to
.IR /var/lib/sb/history.db .
.TP
.B \-\-config\-file \fIPATH\fR
TOML configuration file. Without this option the daemon looks for
.I /etc/sb/sb.toml
and then
.I sb.toml
in the current directory.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Log a heartbeat every five seconds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sb/sb.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sb/history.db
Tiered telemetry history.
.TP
.I /run/sb/sb.sock
Unix socket used by
.BR sb (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sb (1)
